<PARA INFOID = "T080003K071" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "4Apr2005"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Air Conditioner Unit / Air Duct</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>A semi-center mounted integrated air conditioning unit with a thin RS evaporator (RS: Revolutionary Super Slim) and heater core arranged at the front and rear of the unit is used to reduce size. In addition, ventilation resistance inside the unit is reduced and foot space on the front passenger side is ensured.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A "partial recirculation system" that recirculates part of the cabin air in fresh air mode is used to improve heating performance.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A sub-cool condenser and a thin RS evaporator are used to reduce the amount of refrigerant used, giving consideration to the environment.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A wide-angle high-flow defroster, in which the inner wall of the front defroster is shaped radially, is used for excellent defroster performance.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Rear heater ducts are used on cold area specification models to improve comfort for rear seat occupants.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A pollen filter with improved pollen removal efficiency is used as the clean air filter and is provided as standard on all models.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<TITLE>Air Conditioning Unit Layout</TITLE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740076e" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "6.903in" />
</FIGURE>
<INDICATE ID = "T080003K071I01" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Air Duct Layout</TITLE>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740056e" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "6.903in" />
</FIGURE>
